Subject: [PATCH 0005] motion: flags — MotionAgentToggle feature constant
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Purpose
=======
Adds the `MotionAgentToggle` feature to ChromeFeatureList so the autonomous
agent bridge has a kill switch visible in chrome://flags (and remotely
configurable through the standard finch/feature machinery, which Motion uses
ONLY for rollout control — never to weaken security, spec §6).

Gating semantics (see motion/security/SECURITY_NOTES.md):
    agent events flow only when
        ChromeFeatureList.isEnabled("MotionAgentToggle") == true   (this patch)
    AND the user activated the agent in Motion settings
        (MotionAgentBridge.setAgentActive(true) / native runtime state).
    The bridge fails closed: any error resolving the flag disables the agent.

Rebase notes
============
- ChromeFeatureList.java (chrome/browser/flags/android/java/src/org/chromium/
  chrome/browser/flags/) rotates constantly: neighboring constants and the
  sExperiments map are reshuffled every release. The anchors below are
  illustrative; re-anchor at the rebased revision keeping alphabetical
  placement.
- Full chrome://flags visibility also wants a native entry (flag-metadata /
  about_flags); until that lands at rebase, the toggle is controllable via
  `adb shell device_config put chrome android?` is NOT used by Motion — the
  supported paths are: Motion settings UI (Track A parity) and the feature
  being compiled in its default state (disabled until user activation).

Honesty note (spec §77)
=======================
Authored against the upstream file layout as documented for 130.0.6723.58.
NOT verified against a real Chromium checkout — rebase expected.
